  "timestamp": "2026-09-01T19:24:50.515353",
  "headline": "Broadcast SPP, held-out stations: the network kernel is 66% better than knowing nothing but the station's own clock variability, and 60% better than a bulk network average. In the position domain under obstruction (honest, prior sigma = actual error) this is worth 42% at 4 visible satellites and 25% at 8, versus a no-network prior. With a deployable training-estimated sigma the corresponding gains are 54% (4 sats) and 25% (8 sats)."
